{"status":"COMPLETE_SOURCE_API_REVIEW_FINITE_CORE_READY_PARENT_OWNERSHIP_AND_STRICT_ADMISSION_OPEN","source":{"module":"ImbalancedChen.Multiplicity","path":"ImbalancedChen/Multiplicity.lean","sha256":"9d10526b9efe91336095c2bf1ec7fe860fb6e373613b0bf7915c370fb97800a6","LF_lines":210,"bytes":8302,"complete_source_types_bodies_read":true,"direct_imports":["ImbalancedChen.Counting","Mathlib.NumberTheory.AlmostPrime","Mathlib.Tactic.SplitIfs"],"direct_project_parent":{"module":"ImbalancedChen.Counting","source_sha256":"8651960368f560d7c931ef456cdd9bcc8a71477e9bbd5fb9c3add07dcc9206fa","current190_owned":false,"root_reported_readonly_preparation":"six readonly stages PASS; not ownership"}},"prior_review_check":{"bounded_method":"156 source-review JSON files contain exact source SHA; targeted filename/module/content checks found no dedicated complete ImbalancedChen.Multiplicity source/type/body review. Named multiplicity-0f41 and Lichtman multiplicity reviews concern other modules; not reused as this target review. Parent/frontier inventories are not whole-source mathematical review.","matching_complete_prior_target_review_located":false},"written_inventory":{"definitions":3,"theorems":19,"total":22,"serialized_count":null,"note":"Exact written types below are uncompiled written syntax inside namespace ImbalancedChen, with scoped Omega notation. Hashes use UTF8 normalized LF body text after := over indicated lines; all bodies manually read."},"declarations":[{"name":"ImbalancedChen.isSemiprime_iff_exists_primes_mul","lines":[30,44],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem isSemiprime_iff_exists_primes_mul {m : ℕ} :\n    Nat.IsSemiprime m ↔\n      ∃ r q : ℕ, Nat.Prime r ∧ Nat.Prime q ∧ m = r * q","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"a327f9dec99705b0a94736eac9a3de212a188d9c147f0dbf709f981fb200a658","review":"Semiprime unfolds nonzero plus factor-list length2; List.length_eq_two supplies r,q. Each is prime by membership; product reconstruction uses hm:m!=0. Converse stock mul_isAlmostPrime_two. Repeated primes allowed."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.PrimeOrSemiprime.pos","lines":[46,49],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem PrimeOrSemiprime.pos {m : ℕ} (h : PrimeOrSemiprime m) : 0 < m","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"bc43fa9b6f0938484ecc67ee66b0abd7b2168d20d0363eeb475a34dff36327fe","review":"Prime positivity or product of two strictly positive primes; no ordering/distinctness needed."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.PrimeOrSemiprime.cardFactors_eq_one_or_two","lines":[51,55],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem PrimeOrSemiprime.cardFactors_eq_one_or_two {m : ℕ}\n    (h : PrimeOrSemiprime m) : Ω m = 1 ∨ Ω m = 2","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"9b9501eda2f6194c32ad4fb2c83e1221551535f4fdb1c4e4d9f5793606115dbe","review":"Prime has Omega1; product of two primes has Omega2 via stock API. This is multiplicity, not distinct-prime cardinality."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.not_primeOrSemiprime_one","lines":[57,60],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"@[simp] theorem not_primeOrSemiprime_one : ¬ PrimeOrSemiprime 1","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"0e200eb920403b3a13395f75c7bb82187c15397a250f031f1d054979f62ca4b5","review":"Assuming receiver1, preceding Omega1-or2 contradicts stock Omega1=0; no hidden hypothesis."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.cardFactors_le_two_iff_of_pos","lines":[63,77],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem cardFactors_le_two_iff_of_pos {m : ℕ} (hm : 0 < m) :\n    Ω m ≤ 2 ↔ m = 1 ∨ PrimeOrSemiprime m","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"db2a3cc2156678c7f62c51bda24893c45730435b41bd7bed8952b87450f626b8","review":"Positivity hm excludes m=0, essential since Omega0=0. Omega<=2 splits 0/1/2; Omega0 implies0or1, hm removes0; Omega1 iffprime; Omega2 nonzero semiprime bridge. Converse uses Omega1=0 or1or2."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.isAtMostAlmostPrime_two_iff","lines":[81,91],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem isAtMostAlmostPrime_two_iff {m : ℕ} :\n    Nat.IsAtMostAlmostPrime 2 m ↔ m = 1 ∨ PrimeOrSemiprime m","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"c964193c03760c8403109229939f5dde27174f9c4dc9cbe27a38321d2451cde5","review":"Stock at-most predicate explicitly excludes0; convert nonzero to positive, then preceding equivalence. Reverse proves positive fromunit or positiveprime/product, retaining exclusion of0."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.omegaChenPrimes","lines":[97,99],"kind":"def","complete_written_type":"def omegaChenPrimes (N : ℕ) : Finset ℕ","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"1b86f2c78861873dfff87379866913bd1319aeba4daf38c5be50ef88f3906482","review":"Exact Finset.range N filter by Prime p and multiplicity Omega(N-p)<=2. p<N later ensures positive receiver; receiver1 intentionally retained. Not weighted or witness count."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12Omega","lines":[102,102],"kind":"def","complete_written_type":"def D12Omega (N : ℕ) : ℕ","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"8682f2d7bd5d82f6063660a30d23678306803b709dd09faa6aa8b41b267f3704","review":"Natural cardinality of omegaChenPrimes, each additive prime p counted once."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.unitReceiverPrimes","lines":[105,106],"kind":"def","complete_written_type":"def unitReceiverPrimes (N : ℕ) : Finset ℕ","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"b253c9cd15024c8e9ce93f914bc159e233a278d089217d1462b3afc2d1ee05d8","review":"Conditional singleton {N-1} iff Nat.Prime(N-1), empty otherwise. N-1 is truncated natural subtraction; primality ensures N>=3 so singleton really lies below N."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.mem_omegaChenPrimes","lines":[108,111],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"@[simp] theorem mem_omegaChenPrimes {N p : ℕ} :\n    p ∈ omegaChenPrimes N ↔ p < N ∧ Nat.Prime p ∧ Ω (N - p) ≤ 2","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"926e0712196ba4be8117c9209b6ca0a5ca4f28d00a6661262beb8c90e32453fb","review":"Exact filter/range membership equivalence; p<N explicit, no positivity shortcut."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.mem_unitReceiverPrimes","lines":[113,128],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"@[simp] theorem mem_unitReceiverPrimes {N p : ℕ} :\n    p ∈ unitReceiverPrimes N ↔ p < N ∧ Nat.Prime p ∧ N - p = 1","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"abc2444e58822dde6e59315ced1f8dee20f8c6c8f32a531bdaba1a9e329973d8","review":"If Prime(N-1), two_le ensures N-1<N and N-(N-1)=1 by omega, including all small-N boundary cases. Converse from p<N and N-p=1 forces p=N-1. If notprime, the same equality contradicts Prime p."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.omegaChenPrimes_eq_chenPrimes_union","lines":[131,147],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem omegaChenPrimes_eq_chenPrimes_union (N : ℕ) :\n    omegaChenPrimes N = chenPrimes N ∪ unitReceiverPrimes N","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"f5276093fe4ca2c9a272bc1c62adc3beca976449cf592bc8a9b34a3e3a00592b","review":"Pointwise finite partition. p<N gives0<N-p, allowing Omega<=2 bridge. Receiver1 enters singleton branch; prime-or-semiprime enters chenPrimes. Reverse respects positivity and unit Omega0. No factorization witness multiplicity."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.chenPrimes_disjoint_unitReceiverPrimes","lines":[149,156],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem chenPrimes_disjoint_unitReceiverPrimes (N : ℕ) :\n    Disjoint (chenPrimes N) (unitReceiverPrimes N)","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"4be794a8063294eb089c4786ea9db2b45af36e513276427d1ff20360985dbf21","review":"Disjointness from receiver simultaneously PrimeOrSemiprime and equal1; not_primeOrSemiprime_one gives contradiction."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.card_unitReceiverPrimes","lines":[158,161],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"@[simp] theorem card_unitReceiverPrimes (N : ℕ) :\n    (unitReceiverPrimes N).card = if Nat.Prime (N - 1) then 1 else 0","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"b97d5e2ad1045c9beb440681281d73ce1db090c2e5381076e4f701d66a60b475","review":"Conditional singleton/empty cardinality gives exact natural indicator, splitting only Prime(N-1)."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12Omega_eq_D12_add_indicator","lines":[164,170],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem D12Omega_eq_D12_add_indicator (N : ℕ) :\n    D12Omega N = D12 N + (if Nat.Prime (N - 1) then 1 else 0)","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"a60e4f8637aed49b7b0f8cf8a9b2faebf6d84d991097bc44f6f9937d5a5b7d83","review":"Unfold cardinalities, use exact union, disjoint cardinality and singleton indicator. Identity for every natural N."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12Omega_sub_D12_eq_indicator","lines":[172,175],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem D12Omega_sub_D12_eq_indicator (N : ℕ) :\n    D12Omega N - D12 N = if Nat.Prime (N - 1) then 1 else 0","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"a6d0daaf60bf3d6be424b71a8d91fab761ba2be682dce36657a15d8d69af1a51","review":"Natural subtraction exact from additive identity; no hidden negative/truncation loss because D12Omega=D12+indicator."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12_le_D12Omega","lines":[177,179],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem D12_le_D12Omega (N : ℕ) : D12 N ≤ D12Omega N","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"a6d0daaf60bf3d6be424b71a8d91fab761ba2be682dce36657a15d8d69af1a51","review":"Omega count contains D12; direct nonnegative indicator algebra via omega."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12Omega_le_D12_add_one","lines":[181,183],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem D12Omega_le_D12_add_one (N : ℕ) : D12Omega N ≤ D12 N + 1","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"d407a88da5d4504c0d7c914a3d14e5bf158382a036378cceca7a38781172ae25","review":"Indicator is0or1, split_ifs then omega; correct upper bound D12+1."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12Omega_sub_D12_le_one","lines":[185,187],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem D12Omega_sub_D12_le_one (N : ℕ) : D12Omega N - D12 N ≤ 1","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"9770f645d61db30eb08cb37f869790dbbcbf1216184351c763e2f7832ba1ca75","review":"Natural difference <=1 from previous additive upper bound by omega; valid all N."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12Omega_eq_Db_add_B_add_indicator","lines":[190,193],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem D12Omega_eq_Db_add_B_add_indicator (num den N : ℕ) :\n    D12Omega N = Db num den N + B num den N +\n      (if Nat.Prime (N - 1) then 1 else 0)","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"bd2dcac34f0a11df549caadb1ab1538fce7912d400f1a7add300b8d9c9175ab3","review":"Substitute Counting exact D12=Db+B into historical Omega count identity. All num,den,N natural, no rational-exponent or analytic sidecondition."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12Omega_le_Db_add_B_add_one","lines":[195,198],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem D12Omega_le_Db_add_B_add_one (num den N : ℕ) :\n    D12Omega N ≤ Db num den N + B num den N + 1","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"7a015808f1e2f2cf4b451fec63c1d9ca2accb05337388589e934b9b974e8860b","review":"Rewrite Db+B back to D12 and apply historical count upper bound+1; no analytic claim."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12Omega_sub_B_sub_one_le_Db","lines":[202,206],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem D12Omega_sub_B_sub_one_le_Db (num den N : ℕ) :\n    (D12Omega N : ℝ) - (B num den N : ℝ) - 1 ≤ (Db num den N : ℝ)","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_LF":"351b24a901289cdbfbd882c40c956d35189460c0077972a35fe91723dfe9202c","review":"Cast natural upper bound to Real with exact_mod_cast; linarith yields (D12Omega:Real)-(B:Real)-1 <= (Db:Real). Real subtraction untruncated; sign and correction1 retained."}],"manuscript_boundary":{"actual_file":"../chen-imbalanced-semiprimes/paper/source/manuscript-body.tex","actual_sha256":"ee6aecc164cc59f2d1fed1ad9e48f18f98472ab1d77ab425d53d93bc41ce56bd","lines":[18,34,1494,1501],"facts":"Actual current D_{1,2} at22 explicitly requires N-p>1 and counts distinct additive primes. At1495 Db=D12-B; following prose excludes unit and zero, and notes a unit-including convention differs by at most1. Current D12 equals Counting prime-or-semiprime semantics, not D12Omega.","source_comment_scope_issue":"Multiplicity module comments calling D12Omega the manuscript Chen count and saying manuscript convention differs from D12 are historical/stale for this frozen current manuscript. The finite theorems are mathematically valid; do not reinterpret current terminal bounds using D12Omega or impose an unnecessary unit loss. No actual source edit made.","corroboration":"docs/CURRENT_MANUSCRIPT_MAP.md646-648 explicitly says current manuscript excludes unit and terminal usesD12, not historicalD12Omega."},"mathematical_review":{"gap_in_actual_stated_finite_theorems_found":false,"positivity_nonzero":"m>0 required exactly for raw Omega<=2 bridge. At-most-almost-prime excludes0 by definition. p<N makes receiver positive. N=0,1,2 allowed by finite statements; unit singleton empty unless N-1 prime.","multiplicity_and_case":"Omega is ArithmeticFunction.cardFactors (primeFactorsList length). PrimeOrSemiprime includes repeated prime factors and counts no ordering; omegaChenPrimes lowercase set vs D12Omega uppercase natural count are distinct. Finsets count additive p, never factorization witnesses.","subtraction":"Nat subtraction lemmas derive exact additive identity; final Real inequality subtracts B then1 with correct direction. No negative Nat receiver slips in via truncation because membership requires p<N.","analytic_scope":"No PNT/Chen/sieve lowerupper estimate, positive margin or main1+1.75 supplier proved. Historical unit correction does not supply current analytic bounds."},"native_API_sources":[{"file":"Mathlib/NumberTheory/AlmostPrime.lean","sha256":"f06b49c6326bb45f84ed1b00f3591c0300c6837eecfc918b9495278a918f7249","APIs":"IsAlmostPrime40-41: nonzero and Omega=k; IsAtMostAlmostPrime45-46: nonzero and Omega<=k; IsSemiprime49-50; Prime.mul_isAlmostPrime_two83-85. Relevant complete definitions/proofs read."},{"file":"Mathlib/NumberTheory/ArithmeticFunction/Misc.lean","sha256":"412a3138bf47267bf94f01cdafc1234d8d7a85626db7e2f0001d1a1ad40bc3c3","APIs":"cardFactors258-259 primeFactorsList.length; Omega0=0 at269; Omega1=0 at271; zero-iff0or1 at274-275; one-iffprime282-287; apply_prime302-303. Relevant proof bodies read."},{"file":"Mathlib/Data/Nat/Factors.lean","sha256":"3e64e2c8ba907c05209966a7bba8754cf2ab33f328a3010667ffe58c95e0bca3","APIs":"prime_of_mem_primeFactorsList55-64 and prod_primeFactorsList70-81; complete proofs read, product reconstruction explicitly needs n!=0."},{"file":"Mathlib/Data/List/Basic.lean","sha256":"a5490adaf9886c84cf0ffad009267ea9324bfa6c9b81b529454158c19eedd501","APIs":"length_eq_two121-122; exact two-element list decomposition."}],"lexical_safety":{"exact_sorry_axiom_unsafe_admit_code_or_comment_tokens":[],"qualification":"Lexical/source review only; does not certify compiled type/axiom/safety closure."},"original_evidence":{"local_cache_sha256":"34660622ad7c1717b8d8977c4161d5c3db865e87a6e382536b9fef3df6fe7e0a","local_cache":"cache/ImbalancedChen.Multiplicity.json","local_status":"PASS","warnings_as_errors":false,"scope":"Exact-source/direct-object development reuse only","actual_olean_sha256":"2f421673793f153c6dccfcc8463657c8f76d73342f2994e33eb04ed1266ff180","original_takeover_receipt_sha256":"f20be1994587f6a7047ce8e1419e497c91a6baa7159d0b4f4885f75869424bd8","original_takeover_receipt_read":true,"original_command_has_warningAsError":false,"original_exit_code":0,"original_source_before_after_and_object_match":true,"matching_audits_receipt_module_or_source_sha_found":false,"target_in190":false,"PASS_is_not_owned":true},"next_layer_real_preconditions":["Counting must first have exact-source strict/stock complete types/std3/safety evidence and independent root owned acceptance; readonly preparation PASS is insufficient.","After parent is genuinely owned, obtain actual original proper and full native/all5slot/562source/non-target exact input capture; revalidate cache binding especially if Counting object changes. No proper run made here.","Use source-revie